// 3. Save the file and restart `npm run dev`.
//
// Each site object describes ONE of your 5 sites:
//   id        — short slug, no spaces. Used internally + in the dashboard.
//   name      — pretty name (your domain). Shown in the UI.
//   url       — your live production URL.
//   path      — absolute path to the site's repo on your laptop.
//   postsDir  — absolute path to the folder that holds blog post .md files.
//
// For Eleventy sites: postsDir is usually <path>/src/blog/posts
// For Astro sites:    postsDir is usually <path>/src/content/blog
// For Hugo sites:     postsDir is usually <path>/content/posts
// For Jekyll sites:   postsDir is usually <path>/_posts
//
// IMPORTANT: All 5 paths must actually exist on disk before you restart
// Agentic OS, or the SEO tab will show them as missing.

